// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
// specs/t27os/call_session_probe.t27 -- drives call_session.t27 the way a window would: only the cs_* API, one
// cs_poll per pass of its loop, a "person" who answers, reads the code and says match or differ. Not part of the
// app; there is no screen here, so a pass means the session API carries a call, not that a call screen works.
// Runs (one line per check; exit 0 only when every check passed):
//   (no env)               two sessions in this process on 127.0.0.1:47751 / 47752 with the test pattern (no
//                          devices), reused call after call: a full call (ring, answer, the same code on both
//                          sides, ACTIVE, CS_FRAMES frames each way with the caller muted for 50 of them, a forged
//                          plain BYE ignored, hang-up, IDLE), a person who says differ, a decline, a cancel while
//                          ringing, a hang-up while the codes are shown. Bound to 127.0.0.1 the sockets are IPv4
//                          ones (cs_dual_stack) with FD_CLOEXEC, and a dial to an IPv6 is refused.
//   CS_V6=1 (no CS_ROLE)   the same two sessions on the dual-stack socket (call_ip6.t27), bound to :: on 47753 / 47754,
//                          the IPv6 loopback allowed (CS_K_LOOP6, a test aid): a full call to [::1]:47754 (family v6,
//                          every redundant audio copy sent and taken as a datagram of its own, none too big for
//                          IPv6), then a call to 127.0.0.1:47754 on the same sockets (family v4-mapped, no copies alone),
//                          and the refusals (multicast, the loopback without the test aid).
//   CS_ROLE=caller|callee  one side in its own process. CS_BIND / CS_PORT (default 127.0.0.1, caller 47761,
//                          callee 47762), CS_PEER / CS_PEER_PORT (the caller dials there; default 127.0.0.1 and the
//                          other port), CS_FRAMES (200: the caller hangs up once it sent and received that many),
//                          CS_AUDIO=dev (microphone and speakers through AudioQueue on this run loop, volume 0.05)
//                          or test (default), CS_SAY=differ (this person says the codes differ), CS_ANSWER=0 (the
//                          callee never answers), CS_MUTE=1 (the caller mutes frames 100..149), CS_VERIFY_MS,
//                          CS_JB_TARGET / CS_JB_MAX, CS_EXPECT=active (default) or failed. Each side prints
//                          CODE <6 digits>; the operator compares the two logs. Addresses: private networks or 127.x (call_view cv_lan_ok).
//   CS_ROLE=relay          a man in the middle on CS_BIND:CS_PORT that forwards between the first sender and
//                          CS_PEER:CS_PEER_PORT, changes one byte of the callee's ANSWER nonce and puts the hash of
//                          the original ANSWER into the caller's REVEAL (so the callee does not notice): the two
//                          sides then show different codes.
// Build (Apple silicon):
//   t27b build specs/t27os/call_session_probe.t27 -o csp.o --macho
//   ld -arch arm64 -platform_version macos 11.0 $(xcrun --show-sdk-version) -syslibroot $(xcrun --show-sdk-path) \
//      -e _main -lSystem -lffi -framework CoreFoundation -framework Security -framework AudioToolbox \
//      -framework CoreGraphics -framework ImageIO -o csp csp.o
// Test identities only (fixed fingerprints). Refs gHashTag/t27#11560.
